<% content_for(:title, "InstantRecord — What if your Rails app were instant?") %>

<main class="home">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <h1>What if your Rails app were instant?</h1>
    <p class="home-lede">No spinners, no loading states, and it keeps working on a train. InstantRecord is an experimental, open-source Ruby gem that runs your Rails models in the browser, so every click hits a database that’s already here.</p>
    <div class="home-actions">
      <a class="home-button" href="#demos">Try the demos</a>
      <a class="home-button quiet" href="https://github.com/kieranklaassen/instant_record">Read the code on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-how" aria-labelledby="how">
    <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
    <p class="home-sub">The same model file runs in two places. Your server stays the source of truth.</p>
    <div class="home-how-grid">
      <figure class="home-code">
        <figcaption>app/models/issue.rb</figcaption>
<pre><span class="k">class</span> Issue &lt; ApplicationRecord
  <span class="k">include</span> InstantRecord::Syncable

  validates :title, presence: <span class="v">true</span>

  server_only <span class="k">do</span>
    validate :title_allowed_by_server
  <span class="k">end</span>
<span class="k">end</span></pre>
        <p>That one include is the whole opt-in.</p>
      </figure>
      <ol class="home-steps">
        <li><span class="step-mark step-1" aria-hidden="true">1</span><b>Write locally</b><span><code>Issue.create!</code> commits to SQLite in your tab. The page re-renders before the network is involved.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-mark step-2" aria-hidden="true">2</span><b>Queue durably</b><span>The same transaction records a mutation, so a crash, a reload or a dead connection loses nothing.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-mark step-3" aria-hidden="true">3</span><b>Sync in the background</b><span>A loop drains the outbox to your Rails server, which validates and versions every write.</span></li>
        <li><span class="step-mark step-4" aria-hidden="true">4</span><b>Stream everyone else</b><span>Accepted changes come back to every client over server-sent events, and their pages update from local data.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="home-demos-head" id="demos">
    <h2>The demos</h2>
    <span>Six small apps. Open two tabs, or flip Offline at the top right.</span>
  </div>

  <ul class="demo-grid">
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-todo" href="<%= todo_root_path %>">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Todo</h3><span class="card-tag">Optimistic writes</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">Writes land instantly, and a server-only rule can still reject a title after the browser accepted it.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Todo →</span></div>
    </a></li>
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-chat" href="<%= slack_root_path %>">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Chat</h3><span class="card-tag">Channels and threads</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">Channels, DMs and threads, with replies from server-side users arriving over SSE. No WebSocket.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Chat →</span></div>
    </a></li>
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-inbox" href="/email" data-turbo="false">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Inbox</h3><span class="card-tag">Shared mailboxes</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">Reply offline, then switch teammates to see who gets the conversation in Support or Billing.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Inbox →</span></div>
    </a></li>
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-assistant" href="/assistant">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Assistant</h3><span class="card-tag">Streaming replies</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">Ask about your workspace, watch a reply stream in, and pick up any saved conversation later.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Assistant →</span></div>
    </a></li>
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-auth" href="/auth">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Auth</h3><span class="card-tag">Sessions and permissions</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">Sign in as Ada, Ben or Cleo and watch each one’s notes arrive. Sign out, and they leave this browser again.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Auth →</span></div>
    </a></li>
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-migrate" href="<%= migrate_root_path %>">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Ship v2</h3><span class="card-tag">Migrations</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">Fill a local database, leave writes unsynced, then run a migration over the top. Both have to survive.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Ship v2 →</span></div>
    </a></li>
    <li><a class="demo-card demo-card-console" href="<%= console_root_path %>">
      <span class="card-art" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-sheet"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></span>
      <div class="card-body"><div class="card-head"><h3>Console</h3><span class="card-tag">Live ActiveRecord</span></div>
      <p class="card-copy">An ActiveRecord prompt against the database in this tab. Type a query the demo didn’t plan for.</p>
      <span class="go">Open Console →</span></div>
    </a></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="board-band">
    <span>This page was rendered by Rails <%= InstantRecord.browser? ? "inside your browser" : "on the server" %>: <b><%= InstantRecord.browser? ? "Spinel + SQLite" : "CRuby + Postgres" %></b>.</span>
    <a href="<%= receipts_path %>">What this cost on your device: performance receipts →</a>
  </div>

  <footer class="project-strip">
    <p>InstantRecord is an MIT-licensed Ruby gem. Every page here is in the repo, and View source reads it out of the app that just rendered it.</p>
    <p class="project-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/kieranklaassen/instant_record">GitHub</a>
      <a href="https://rubygems.org/gems/instant_record">RubyGems</a>
      <code>gem "instant_record"</code>
    </p>
  </footer>
</main>
